NeoSCAD patch to manifold-rust 0.15.0 (crates.io): a batch_boolean round's
pairs run side by side, as in C++ (csg_tree.cpp:451-479), and go back on
the heap in pair order with the serials the sequential loop gave them, so
the output is the sequential output. After each round the mesh IDs its
booleans reserved are renumbered in pair order
(renumber_round_mesh_ids), so the IDs, and the run order of a later
disjoint union, do not depend on which pair drew from the counter first.
The crate's csg_tree tests move to src/csg_tree_tests.rs. Tests:
crates/geom/tests/parallel_kernels.rs, and the crate's own
(src/csg_tree_tests.rs).

Upstream: proposed as branch `neoscad/parallel-batch-rounds`
(commit e086ef9, larsbrubaker/manifold-rust#7) of a fork of
larsbrubaker/manifold-rust, on top of its
`main` at 9989b92 (0.15.0 plus two QuickHull commits and a regression
test for unions, which touch none of these files). This patch is that commit's changes under src/, byte for
byte apart from CRLF line endings; the branch also adds a benchmark
under examples/ and a note in docs/, which are not vendored.

Apply from the crate root on top of 0003: patch -p1 < this file.
The crate's older sources use CRLF line endings; files this series
adds use LF.
See vendor/README.md ("The parallel boolean patch").

